  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jack Perkins lasted 3.2 innings and Miami buried them early. The A's never recovered from a six-run first.",
    "what_this_means": "Trailing from the opening inning changes everything. The offense woke up in the third and fourth, scratching out five runs across two innings, but they were chasing a game that was already decided. Nick Kurtz drove in two with a solo shot, and Carlos Cortes contributed hits, but the damage was done. Mason Barnett gave up four runs in two innings. The bullpen couldn't plug a hole that size. Perkins got out of there too early and handed the game to a pen that wasn't ready for it. When you fall behind 6\u20130 before your starter finishes the fourth, the math doesn't work. You're not coming back from that in this division. Chasing leads this early is a luxury they can't afford.",
